    <briefdescription>
<para>Zero-copy view of a single time-series row for high-throughput batch ingestion. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Unlike <computeroutput><ref refid="structthemis_1_1_t_s_store_1_1_data_point" kindref="compound">DataPoint</ref></computeroutput>, all string fields are <computeroutput>std::string_view</computeroutput> — no heap allocation is required at the call site. The caller must ensure that the backing storage for <computeroutput><ref refid="structthemis_1_1_t_s_store_1_1_t_s_row_1a757a0257ada9d4cacb9902e46529668a" kindref="member">metric</ref></computeroutput> and <computeroutput><ref refid="structthemis_1_1_t_s_store_1_1_t_s_row_1ae57d18672ae2df469e0cc80f765a25c5" kindref="member">entity</ref></computeroutput> outlives the <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1_t_s_store_1a2b54cb6bf7aeb4a1429a5e0fc6ce3f26" kindref="member">putBatch()</ref></computeroutput> call.</para>
<para><computeroutput>tags</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>metadata</computeroutput> are optional JSON blobs; pass an empty / null JSON value when not needed. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
